From f8bbe1005756351a195a4aac2ffe8944279272d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saulo Vallory <saulovallory@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:23:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] docs(readme): a beta note says the API may change until 1.0.0

The npm beta publishes plain 0.1.0 on the latest dist-tag (operator decision, 2026-10-09), so every published package README carries the same one-line beta note right after its intro. This README had no earlier alpha warning to replace; the note sits between the intro paragraph and the grammar description.
---
 README.md | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 5ed06f6..7caee9f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@ its highlight and injection queries, the compiled wasm, and a
 [docmd](https://docmd.io/) plugin that highlights `` ```mx `` fences at build
 time.
 
+> **Beta.** This package is at 0.x. Its API may change in any release until 1.0.0.
+
 MX is Marko's syntax plus the decision 146 name sugar (`#id`, `.class` and
 `:name` anywhere in a tag) and decision 156 atoms (`:name` as a value:
 `default=:draft`, `accept=[:title, :body]`, `self.status === :sent`).
-- 
2.55.0

